The 18-month / 18,000-mile window is a lemon-law presumption, not a requirement. It does not decide whether you have a good case. What matters is whether the defect first occurred during the original manufacturer warranty. If the defect is reported to the manufacturer within the terms of the warranty, your lemon law claim is valid.

When you file a claim, your Sacramento lemon law attorney will fight for, including:

